:["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3235,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py:217 `os.environ[\"REBAR_SYNC_PUSH\"] = \"off\"` (subscript assignment)","src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py:393 `os.environ.pop(\"REBAR_SYNC_PUSH\", None)` (pre-existing pop, restore path)","src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py:395 `os.environ[\"REBAR_SYNC_PUSH\"] = _prev_push`","AC-2: 'An os.environ access the recogniser does not understand causes a LOUD failure'","Plan's investigation lists only hypothetical forms ('an os.environ alias bound to a local name, a dict(os.environ) copy') and does not name these concrete pre-existing assignment/pop sites"],"finding":"The fail-closed remedy (AC-2: 'an os.environ access the recogniser does not understand causes a LOUD failure') would newly implicate pre-existing os.environ ASSIGNMENT and restore sites the plan does not enumerate. src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py contains os.environ['REBAR_SYNC_PUSH'] = 'off' (line 217), os.environ.pop('REBAR_SYNC_PUSH', None) (line 393), and os.environ['REBAR_SYNC_PUSH'] = _prev_push (line 395) — accesses that are writes/cleanup, not reads-to-document. A generator that fail-closes on any unrecognised os.environ access would fail the build on this untouched file unless it distinguishes reads from writes/restores.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f593a7a91d755cec3","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Investigation before choosing a remedy' + AC line 2","norm_id":"ne330f4d7f8c97724","priority":0.4765,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adopts the fail-closed AC-2 recogniser; the build fails on import_ndjson.py's subscript assignments and restore-pop even though the ticket never touches that file","Widen-recogniser approach registers import_ndjson.py:393's pop harmlessly (key already registered via line 216 os.environ.get) — but the plan does not confirm this, leaving whether the key count moves unverified"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the investigation section, add import_ndjson.py's os.environ['REBAR_SYNC_PUSH'] assignments (:217,:395) and os.environ.pop restore (:393) as concrete forms already present, and specify that the fail-closed recogniser scopes its error to READ expressions (get/pop/subscript-load) only — not Store/assignment targets or already-recognised keys — so widening/fail-closing does not implicate those sites.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: reasonable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the fail-closed guard behaves for env reads whose receiver is NOT the literal `os.environ` attribute (aliased binding, `dict(os.environ)` copy — the latter live at _bridge_runner.py:198), since `_is_os_environ` only matches `os.environ` on a bare `os` Name; either extend detection to those forms or record why they are out of scope so the 'no silent omission' AC is honest about its boundary.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gen_env_registry.py:60-67 `_is_os_environ` requires `node.value` to be `ast.Name` with `id == 'os'`","src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py:198 `active_environ = dict(os.environ if environ is None else environ)` — an existing non-`os.environ.<attr>` read shape","Plan Investigation section lists 'an os.environ alias bound to a local name, a dict(os.environ) copy' as forms to establish","Fail-closed detection scoped to 'os.environ attribute access' cannot fire on an aliased receiver, since alias reads do not match the attribute pattern"],"finding":"The fail-closed remedy (AC line 2) is scoped to 'an os.environ access the recogniser does not understand', but the generator's `_is_os_environ` (lines 60-67) only recognises `os.environ` when its value is a bare `Name` with id `os`. An aliased binding (`environ = os.environ; environ.pop(...)`) or a `dict(os.environ)` copy — the latter already exists at `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py:198`, and both are named in the plan's own investigation list — never enters that attribute branch, so a guard keyed on `os.environ.<attr>` would still silently miss alias-based reads. The plan should confirm the fail-closed check's trigger boundary covers (or explicitly excludes with rationale) the alias/copy form, otherwise the fail-closed AC does not fully deliver the 'no silent omission' guarantee it promises.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1d5de2855697eb18","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, line 2 ('An os.environ access the recogniser does not understand causes a LOUD failure'); cross-ref Investigation section","norm_id":"nd6c17d4146deffe1","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future contributor writes `env = os.environ` then `env.get('REBAR_NEW')`, expecting the fail-closed guard to either register or error, but the read is silently dropped and no build fails","The existing `dict(os.environ)` at _bridge_runner.py:198 is used to reach a key that never appears in docs/env-vars.md and no LOUD failure fires"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"9774eb7fb6801033","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["3302dffdbcca2fcd",4344],"des